        ("Age stereotypes", "Beliefs about older people, positive (wise) or negative (frail, forgetful), absorbed from culture."),
        ("Stereotype embodiment theory", "Becca Levy's theory that age stereotypes absorbed across life become self-stereotypes that affect health."),
        ("Self-perceptions of aging", "How people view their own aging; positive views predict better health outcomes."),
        ("7.5 years", "Levy's widely cited finding: older adults with positive age beliefs lived about 7.5 years longer than those with negative beliefs."),
